# Article: Pack (adversaries, human integration gate)

Roles: coder, reviewer.

Chain: coder -> reviewer -> coder.

- coder implements a slice in the candidate worktree, then sends a
  git_handoff to reviewer.
- reviewer adversarially reviews the merged result. Findings that require
  changes go back to coder as a git_handoff carrying the review commit;
  that handoff continues the chain (coder fixes and re-forwards to
  reviewer).
- A clean review's return handoff is TERMINAL: coder merges it into the
  candidate branch and stops.
- Neither role integrates or pushes the candidate to the project root's
  protected branch. The operator verifies the terminal candidate and
  presents it for human review. Only the operator integrates it after the
  human explicitly approves.
